# What must NOT go into the image.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT OPTIONAL, and it is not a copy of .gitignore.
# `docker build` reads .dockerignore; it has never heard of .gitignore. A
# repo with a flawless .gitignore will still bake .env into an image via
# `COPY . .` - and `docker history` shows it to anyone who pulls that
# image. Two different tools, two different files, one shared mistake.
#
# The rule: start by excluding everything you cannot justify shipping.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets - the reason this file exists
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.streamlit/secrets.toml
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local environment - large, and WRONG for the image
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .venv holds Windows binaries; the image is Linux. Copying it in would
# both bloat the image and shadow the correctly-installed packages.
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operational data - contains real customer messages
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
runs/
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development-only. Excluded because every file in the image is a file
# that must be patched when it has a CVE.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
tests/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.vscode/
.idea/
assets/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, though it may look like it should be:
#
#   docs/      the RAG corpus - the policy agent has nothing to cite
#              without it. It is DATA, not documentation.
#   db/*.sql   schema + grants, needed to re-seed a fresh database.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
